# Round 97: the width lens, one helper family over. Round 96 taught the
# INDEX helpers the VM's int-width integer test and left the SLICE family
# at long width -- so every exact double in (INT_MAX, LONG_MAX] passed
# here and failed there, and aot_slice_any then TRUNCATED the value its
# own test had just admitted (int orig_start = (int)si). Testing at one
# width and storing at another is why this was silent-wrong rather than
# merely mis-messaged: the truncated 0 sailed through the range check.
#
#   sum of xs[-4294967296 : 3]   VM raises rc 1;  AOT printed 60, rc 0
#   sum of xs[0 : 4294967296]    VM raises rc 1;  AOT printed 0,  rc 0
#
# The bound is computed at runtime here (doubling in a loop) so the
# fixture pins the RUNTIME path, not a literal-emission artifact -- the
# one existing slice-bound fixture uses 9, entirely inside int.
xs is [10, 20, 30]
k is 1
i is 0
loop while i < 32:
    k is k * 2
    i is i + 1
print of k
print of "before"
print of (sum of xs[0 : k])
print of "after"
